# Declared in `../beans.json` as the `merge-queue` node, and empty until a
# merge steward records a decision.
#
# Same reason as `workflows/.gitkeep`: git does not track an empty directory,
# and a declared-but-absent directory is the bean `dh4f` defect — a consumer
# fans out over the declaration, scans nothing, and reports a clean run over
# it.
#
# Empty ON PURPOSE rather than seeded. An entry records a decision a steward
# actually made, with its reason and its author; inventing one to make the
# directory look used would put a fabricated decision into the graph that
# every later reader would take for a real one. The kind's whole discipline is
# that a stored value is a decision somebody owns.
#
# What goes here: one JSON file per open pull request under consideration,
# carrying `"$schema": "folio-merge-queue-entry/v1"` and validating against
# `MergeQueueEntrySchema`. Never a fact GitHub owns — CI, mergeability,
# labels and the head SHA are read live and refused by name.
